WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:10.940
Through me the way is to the city dolent;
Through me the way is to eternal dole;
Through me the way among the people lost.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:18.950
Justice incited my sublime Creator;
Created me divine omnipotence;
The highest Wisdom and the primal Love.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:27.990
Before me there were no created things,
Only eterne, and I eternal last.
All hope abandon, ye who enter here!

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:10.170
He will come soon.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.400
Bringing with him
a hundred million origins...

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:20.580
Bringing with him
a hundred million demises...

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.580
To carry out his revenge of
one hundred million grudges.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:15.880
You bastard!

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.040
Die!

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:09.980
Do you know Tri-Edge?

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.430
How deplorable.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.070
It's become a serious problem,
what with these PKs running rampant...

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.330
throughout the network game
"The World".

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:36.570
PK...Player Killer?

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:37.650
Right.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:42.680
They will bully any weak,
or innocent characters and kill them.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:44.550
- A detestable bunch.
- H-Hey!

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:50.790
And then there is the PKK who seeks to
crush the PKs with his own power.

00:04:51.220 --> 00:04:56.490
He may act as if he's on the side of justice,
but his true nature differs little from a PK.

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.600
But why...?

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:06.840
Doesn't he realize that making others suffer
only causes pain in your own heart?

00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:14.280
Who knows? I still can't understand
what's going on in their heads.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:22.790
The black PKK that reeks of blood.
The "Terror of Death".

00:05:23.120 --> 00:05:27.320
I see. I suppose
rumors can be quite helpful.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:31.360
So, are those fangs of yours real?

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:32.660
Haseo?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:38.200
That's the sort of man you'd call a PK.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.240
They're all so shallow.

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:45.510
Excuse me!
Why do you commit PKs?

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:47.750
- Do you ever consider the victim's...?
- Look!

00:05:53.750 --> 00:05:55.020
Shino?!

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:58.750
Atoli.

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:02.220
Do you know him?

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.560
No.

00:06:06.100 --> 00:06:07.730
Atoli?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.430
I think you've got the wrong person.

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:17.970
It's not unusual to run into others of
the same PC model in a network game.

00:06:18.070 --> 00:06:20.940
Huh?

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:31.650
<i>I received a short mail?
Who could it be?</i>

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:55.210
Ovan!

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:04.850
It's been a long time, Haseo...
not since the Brigade was shut down.

00:07:05.920 --> 00:07:07.490
Six months...

00:07:08.590 --> 00:07:12.060
What have you been doing
for six months?!

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.170
Seems that you've gotten much stronger,
Haseo.

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:21.140
Don't avoid the question!
You disappeared and the Brigade fell apart!

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:24.510
You disappeared and Shino was PKed!

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:26.910
You disappeared and I...

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:28.340
Became the Terror of Death.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:33.180
In order to avenge the death of Shino.

00:07:34.650 --> 00:07:36.120
Tri-Edge.

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:52.100
I understand that that is
the name of the PC who PKed Shino.

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:57.510
And even now, she remains in
an unexplained coma.

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:02.080
How do you know all that?

00:08:02.180 --> 00:08:06.080
You think I spent the past six months
doing nothing?

00:08:08.020 --> 00:08:10.620
So then, you've been...

00:08:10.790 --> 00:08:15.190
Yes. I've been trying to figure out
how to get Shino back.

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:25.900
Haseo, do you have
the courage to face Tri-Edge?

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.140
What?

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:36.580
If my findings prove to be correct,
he will return today.

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:42.220
Here, to this stage of tragedy.

00:08:45.050 --> 00:08:49.420
He's going to come back?

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:55.760
This is something
that can only be entrusted to you.

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:50.750
Shino!

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:56.020
Hang in there! Hey!

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:13.040
Shino!

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.750
N-No...No! Not this!

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:21.420
No way!
This can't be!

00:10:28.890 --> 00:10:32.230
Please don't cry.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:39.370
You're a man...

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:41.500
Shino!

00:10:44.510 --> 00:10:47.180
Ovan...

00:10:48.710 --> 00:10:52.580
Please save Ovan...

00:10:54.850 --> 00:10:56.520
Save Ovan?

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:25.180
Shino!

00:11:35.720 --> 00:11:37.390
What was that sound?

00:12:07.020 --> 00:12:08.460
<i>You're him...</i>

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:11.390
<i>...the one from back then!</i>

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:19.400
I finally found you!

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:22.900
You're the one!
You're the one who killed Shino!

00:12:25.810 --> 00:12:30.080
Tri-Edge!

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.970
What is this? Level 1?!
How can that be?!

00:14:39.140 --> 00:14:40.580
No way...

00:14:41.140 --> 00:14:43.140
Tri-Edge!

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:45.880
Did I lose?

00:14:46.410 --> 00:14:48.220
Damn!

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:53.560
Damn! Damn! Damn! Damn! Damn!

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.760
Damn!

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:15.310
What is this place?

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:19.810
Welcome to the Serpent of Lore...

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:22.680
Haseo.

00:15:27.020 --> 00:15:29.260
Who the hell are you guys?

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.890
We are Project G.U.

00:15:33.960 --> 00:15:38.500
We are a special task force team
that was set up by the CC Corporation.

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:42.470
You mean, you're the administrators
of this game?

00:15:43.170 --> 00:15:46.510
You could think of us that way.

00:15:47.810 --> 00:15:49.740
Take a look at this.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:56.320
A supernatural phenomenon
has been detected in various Areas.

00:15:56.650 --> 00:16:00.790
We have been calling
these occurrences collectively as AIDA.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:06.090
Our task is to determine
what's been causing this AIDA.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.130
I suppose you're a victim of it as well.

00:16:09.500 --> 00:16:10.870
I am?

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.740
Are you talking about Tri-Edge?!

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:14.700
Hm.

00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:21.280
It's a serious situation.
There are victims all over the world.

00:16:21.410 --> 00:16:25.250
One hundred and twelve victims
have been confirmed so far.

00:16:25.350 --> 00:16:30.020
Each of these victims
have fallen into unexplained comas...

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:32.790
...with no prospect of awakening
from them.

00:16:33.460 --> 00:16:34.820
Sh-Shino!

00:16:37.490 --> 00:16:41.530
That's right.
She is also a victim of AIDA.

00:16:41.630 --> 00:16:46.000
Our goal is to eliminate this phenomenon.

00:16:46.230 --> 00:16:51.340
Our desires seem to match.
Don't you think, Haseo?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:58.050
So you want me to cooperate?
It sounds too convenient to me.

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:00.520
Besides, why do you need me?

00:17:01.080 --> 00:17:04.990
There's a secret power hidden in your PC.

00:17:05.090 --> 00:17:08.390
It's the only power that can counter AIDA.

00:17:08.860 --> 00:17:10.330
Power...

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:17.130
It hasn't revealed itself yet,
but once you awaken to it...

00:17:17.400 --> 00:17:19.170
I can defeat Tri-Edge?!

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:21.670
He'll be no match for you.

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:26.140
We have a name for those
who possess that power:

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:28.880
Epitaph User.

00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:30.780
Epitaph User?

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:33.920
Don't you want it, Haseo?

00:17:34.350 --> 00:17:36.420
That power?

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:43.960
<i>So, what am I supposed to do?</i>

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:46.490
<i>Do you want to get stronger?</i>

00:17:46.590 --> 00:17:50.700
<i>- Stronger! Stronger! Stronger! Stronger!
- Of course! I need more power!</i>

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:53.200
That's fine.

00:17:55.300 --> 00:17:56.940
- It's not enough!
- Mind <i>is</i> power.

00:17:57.570 --> 00:18:02.440
True strength is only realized
when it is born of a strong will.

00:18:04.010 --> 00:18:07.520
<i>It is to believe and think.</i>

00:18:08.450 --> 00:18:14.690
<i>It is about how you use your power
in order to accomplish your objectives.</i>

00:18:15.620 --> 00:18:19.730
<i>If only...If only I had power...!</i>

00:18:33.580 --> 00:18:36.480
You're no match for me!
Not even close!

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:40.450
W-Wait! I'm not done yet...
Damn...

00:18:40.680 --> 00:18:44.150
Damn! Why?!
Why won't my power reveal itself?!

00:18:44.820 --> 00:18:47.590
I need that power!

00:18:53.390 --> 00:18:57.030
Tri-Edge!

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:21.720
D-Damn...

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:26.330
Um...

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.670
Wait, Haseo!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.400
What?

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:39.810
Would you like to exchange
member addresses?

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:40.780
Huh?

00:19:43.650 --> 00:19:45.180
Um...

00:19:46.510 --> 00:19:48.850
When I saw you the other day...

00:19:49.280 --> 00:19:53.420
...I felt like I wanted to talk to you
some more!

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.690
Talk?

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:00.930
With you?

00:20:04.530 --> 00:20:07.440
Because you seem so sad.

00:20:13.680 --> 00:20:17.010
Because you have such a tortured look...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:20.720
...I thought maybe there was something
I could do.

00:20:23.220 --> 00:20:24.590
Gimme a break!

00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:29.060
W-Wait! Haseo!

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:39.330
I see no sign of Haseo
awakening to his power any time soon.

00:20:40.640 --> 00:20:42.100
Master Yata?

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:50.410
Haseo seems to be with her a lot lately.

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:56.750
Her presence within him
is growing significantly.

00:20:57.790 --> 00:21:02.360
You think that the time he spends with her
has been dampening his urge for revenge?

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:07.000
Yes. I can't help but think
it'll prevent his awakening.

00:21:09.200 --> 00:21:11.030
There's no problem.

00:21:13.130 --> 00:21:16.670
What's necessary for the awakening
is a hunger for power...

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:19.240
...a psychological shock...

00:21:19.310 --> 00:21:24.950
...and the release of a pure spirit.

00:21:27.380 --> 00:21:29.980
I'm sure his madness is pure.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.690
However, right now, that's...

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:33.990
There's no need to worry.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:36.360
May I ask why?

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:38.390
That man.

00:21:43.030 --> 00:21:46.830
If there was any danger of Haseo
losing his power...

00:21:47.040 --> 00:21:49.570
...that man would most definitely
make his move.

00:21:50.200 --> 00:21:53.810
And yet, he's remained silent.

00:21:55.140 --> 00:21:58.680
That means that nothing of importance
has changed for the moment.

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.350
Then what about us?

00:22:01.520 --> 00:22:05.120
We should simply continue to observe him.

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:09.790
And watch the darkness of his soul.

00:22:19.600 --> 00:22:22.700
You did it!
I'm impressed, Haseo.

00:22:23.540 --> 00:22:26.340
I can do a lot better.

00:22:26.510 --> 00:22:28.580
I am going to get stronger!

00:22:28.680 --> 00:22:29.980
And...!

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.730
Um, Haseo?

00:22:35.730 --> 00:22:36.380
Huh?

00:22:39.250 --> 00:22:43.160
Is there a purpose to getting stronger?

00:22:51.130 --> 00:22:55.040
Obviously I'd want to get stronger
in a network game.

00:22:55.270 --> 00:22:59.240
But there is no real goal in being strong.

00:23:02.410 --> 00:23:04.610
Sometimes you have to stop and
notice the flowers growing by your feet...

00:23:04.710 --> 00:23:08.720
...or the beautiful scenery.

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:13.790
I think it's important to enjoy your encounters
within The World as well.

00:23:14.020 --> 00:23:17.790
I'm sure of it.

00:23:20.930 --> 00:23:22.460
Encounters?

00:23:23.830 --> 00:23:26.200
Stop and notice the flowers?

00:23:33.810 --> 00:23:36.780
Impossible! No way!

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:42.020
Are you stupid or something?

00:23:46.520 --> 00:23:48.460
I'll show you...

00:23:51.890 --> 00:23:54.430
I'll show you what this really is!

00:23:56.400 --> 00:24:00.440
Listen! This here is nothing but data!

00:24:00.570 --> 00:24:04.440
Just texture pasted onto polygons!
Just fake!

00:24:04.570 --> 00:24:08.810
How can you say that
this made up fake world is "beautiful"?!

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:11.210
H-Haseo...

00:24:11.310 --> 00:24:16.220
The only thing that's real in The World
is the player!

00:24:16.650 --> 00:24:20.150
You get stronger and attack other players.

00:24:20.320 --> 00:24:22.920
That's how we all connect!

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:25.960
That's how the game works!

00:24:26.060 --> 00:24:29.100
You got a problem with that?!
Answer me!

00:24:29.200 --> 00:24:31.170
Tell me what's wrong with it!

00:24:32.300 --> 00:24:33.600
But...!

00:24:35.740 --> 00:24:37.000
Go home.

00:24:37.040 --> 00:24:38.520
What?!

00:24:38.610 --> 00:24:43.740
You're a distraction! Don't ever show
your face around me again!

00:24:56.120 --> 00:24:57.330
Damn...

00:24:58.960 --> 00:25:03.600
I wish you wouldn't say all that
with Shino's face.

00:25:35.260 --> 00:25:37.470
I really am useless.

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:40.640
Atoli, isn't it?

00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:45.610
Who are you?

00:25:46.570 --> 00:25:49.640
Is Haseo the cause of your troubles?

00:25:51.480 --> 00:25:54.620
Are you an acquaintance of Haseo's?

00:25:55.420 --> 00:25:56.920
I'm a close friend.

00:26:02.690 --> 00:26:06.590
I'm really no good.

00:26:09.030 --> 00:26:12.930
Whatever I do,
I end up irritating someone.

00:26:13.770 --> 00:26:17.470
Even in the real world,
I'm always on the outside...

00:26:17.570 --> 00:26:19.770
...or being completely ignored.

00:26:22.040 --> 00:26:24.450
I did try hard.

00:26:25.980 --> 00:26:29.820
I really did try hard.

00:26:31.620 --> 00:26:37.120
It wasn't working out for me in the real world,
so that's why I came to the network.

00:26:38.090 --> 00:26:41.400
Atoli, can I tell you something?

00:26:43.930 --> 00:26:46.130
About how to get along with Haseo?

00:26:46.870 --> 00:26:49.640
How to get along with him?

00:26:50.470 --> 00:26:51.670
Yes.

00:26:56.210 --> 00:26:57.410
Listen...

00:27:02.720 --> 00:27:05.050
Atoli disappeared?!

00:27:07.560 --> 00:27:09.020
Look.

00:27:09.720 --> 00:27:14.900
After she transported from the Town
to a certain Area, we lost track of her.

00:27:15.470 --> 00:27:17.840
We know where she was headed...

00:27:17.840 --> 00:27:24.340
...but even with our monitoring program,
there's no way to observe her.

00:27:28.510 --> 00:27:31.350
It appears she's deviated
from her PC specs.

00:27:33.650 --> 00:27:35.720
Must be the AIDA phenomenon.

00:27:36.820 --> 00:27:38.020
Damn!

00:27:39.390 --> 00:27:42.260
So, where's the last Area
she transported to?!

00:28:07.450 --> 00:28:09.880
<i>You must find Tri-Edge.</i>

00:28:09.980 --> 00:28:13.920
<i>That'll prove your feelings for Haseo,
and I'm sure he'll reciprocate...</i>

00:28:18.660 --> 00:28:19.890
Atoli!

00:28:20.900 --> 00:28:22.230
Haseo?

00:28:23.000 --> 00:28:26.990
- How did you know to come here?
- What are you doing in a place like this?

00:28:26.990 --> 00:28:29.140
No! Stay away!

00:28:31.750 --> 00:28:36.120
I will do what I can with my own power
to track down Tri-Edge!

00:28:36.940 --> 00:28:38.090
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:28:38.910 --> 00:28:42.120
Why do you know about Tri-Edge?

00:28:44.120 --> 00:28:47.520
I heard all about it from Mr. Ovan.

00:28:47.760 --> 00:28:51.330
He said that you lost someone
very precious to you.

00:28:52.360 --> 00:28:56.030
And that my PC model is exactly like her.

00:28:58.000 --> 00:29:01.570
Is that why you always look so tortured?

00:29:01.670 --> 00:29:05.810
Is that why you seem so sad
when you look at me?

00:29:07.780 --> 00:29:11.850
The world is right here!
And it carries on!

00:29:12.150 --> 00:29:16.850
Your world is always with you, Haseo!

00:29:21.190 --> 00:29:24.730
I will always be here too.

00:29:25.260 --> 00:29:28.200
I will always be watching you from here!

00:29:28.930 --> 00:29:32.100
So please smile, Haseo!

00:29:33.130 --> 00:29:37.710
And please see me, and the world!

00:29:38.670 --> 00:29:40.270
Atoli...

00:29:58.290 --> 00:29:59.660
Tri-Edge!

00:30:07.640 --> 00:30:10.280
Ahh...

00:30:12.710 --> 00:30:14.310
It was you...

00:30:16.480 --> 00:30:19.880
You're to blame...!

00:30:20.650 --> 00:30:25.950
I lost the Brigade, Shino, and everything!

00:30:28.060 --> 00:30:31.830
Tri-Edge!

00:31:12.070 --> 00:31:14.170
Wait, Haseo!
I think it best to...!

00:31:14.270 --> 00:31:17.140
Hold it. I think he can handle it now.

00:31:18.010 --> 00:31:19.070
It'll awaken.

00:31:36.690 --> 00:31:40.630
It's coming...it's coming...!
It's coming!

00:31:41.860 --> 00:31:45.600
Skeith!

00:32:09.520 --> 00:32:11.860
Answer me, Tri-Edge!

00:32:12.190 --> 00:32:14.190
Tell me how to get Shino back!

00:32:28.580 --> 00:32:30.050
Damn!

00:32:37.280 --> 00:32:39.890
If you won't say...

00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:45.430
...I'll strike right into your soul!

00:33:53.290 --> 00:33:55.000
Damn...

00:33:56.260 --> 00:33:58.730
I can't move...

00:34:09.680 --> 00:34:11.680
Is this it for me?

00:34:46.750 --> 00:34:49.980
Take this!

00:35:25.950 --> 00:35:27.190
Wait!

00:35:27.820 --> 00:35:29.860
Tell me how to return Shino
to the way she was!

00:35:39.930 --> 00:35:40.930
Damn!

00:35:49.540 --> 00:35:50.480
Atoli...

00:35:57.820 --> 00:35:59.190
Look...

00:36:11.930 --> 00:36:13.170
<i>What is it?</i>

00:36:21.410 --> 00:36:23.810
Atoli! Get away from there!

00:36:24.110 --> 00:36:25.150
Huh?

00:37:08.890 --> 00:37:12.960
Atoli!

00:37:41.360 --> 00:37:44.990
Where...?

00:37:46.690 --> 00:37:48.260
Where...am I?

00:37:48.700 --> 00:37:50.760
Where am I?

00:37:50.860 --> 00:37:53.230
<i>Don't you think she's totally annoying?</i>

00:37:53.900 --> 00:37:58.270
<i>- She's so lame, and she stinks, too.
- Let's ignore her.</i>

00:37:58.910 --> 00:38:03.880
<i>- You know, girls should be reserved.
- How about dressing more discreetly?</i>

00:38:06.150 --> 00:38:08.780
<i>Don't you think she's so uncool?</i>

00:38:08.880 --> 00:38:12.520
<i>Who does she think she is,
in this day and age? Seriously. Yikes!</i>

00:38:13.500 --> 00:38:15.090
N-No...!

00:38:15.390 --> 00:38:19.580
<i>She was looking at us.
Maybe she has the hots for you!</i>

00:38:19.580 --> 00:38:23.700
- <i>Whoa! Gimme a break!</i>
- Stop...! N-No! No! No!

00:38:23.700 --> 00:38:27.400
<i>- Your friends are your friends, not you.</i>
- No! No!

00:38:27.400 --> 00:38:30.970
<i>I mean, seriously,
you are too annoying!</i>

00:38:36.290 --> 00:38:40.160
No!

00:38:44.450 --> 00:38:45.590
Atoli!

00:38:46.450 --> 00:38:50.290
Hey! Atoli!
Atoli!

00:38:50.790 --> 00:38:52.560
Wake up!

00:38:53.060 --> 00:38:56.760
Atoli! Atoli!

00:38:56.930 --> 00:39:00.630
I've confirmed the partial destruction of
PC data as a result of AIDA.

00:39:01.030 --> 00:39:04.840
At this rate, not only will the PC be lost
but perhaps the player herself as well.

00:39:05.470 --> 00:39:09.410
I can deal with that with my power!

00:39:09.510 --> 00:39:10.440
Hang on!

00:39:11.240 --> 00:39:13.710
An Epitaph user's power
is too dangerous.

00:39:14.010 --> 00:39:15.680
Why?!

00:39:15.680 --> 00:39:17.420
If I don't hurry, Atoli will be...!

00:39:17.520 --> 00:39:20.420
You can't, Haseo!
Take a good look.

00:39:21.290 --> 00:39:24.690
Atoli's PC is very unstable right now.

00:39:25.530 --> 00:39:29.630
If you force your power onto her,
we could lose her in the real world as well.

00:39:30.830 --> 00:39:32.700
Then what am I supposed to do?!

00:39:36.170 --> 00:39:37.870
There's one way.

00:39:40.240 --> 00:39:43.910
You and Atoli share your PCs.

00:39:44.780 --> 00:39:49.050
That way, you can let Atoli
utilize your power.

00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:52.120
That's right.
If you do that...

00:39:52.450 --> 00:39:55.160
Hang on! That's reckless!

00:39:55.260 --> 00:39:57.390
One mistake and Haseo will also
become a Lost One...!

00:39:57.490 --> 00:39:58.560
I'll do it!

00:39:58.660 --> 00:39:59.860
Haseo?

00:40:00.530 --> 00:40:02.330
I'll do it!

00:40:02.430 --> 00:40:03.860
Pi, give him support.

00:40:03.960 --> 00:40:04.930
Yes.

00:40:16.610 --> 00:40:18.850
<i>Don't you think she's so uncool?</i>

00:40:18.950 --> 00:40:21.950
Stay focused!
What're you doing?!

00:40:33.890 --> 00:40:35.030
AIDA!

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:38.670
It seems our intervention's
been detected.

00:40:53.980 --> 00:40:55.120
What is it?

00:40:55.220 --> 00:40:56.680
Intruder detected!

00:40:56.780 --> 00:40:59.320
It appears to be trying to interfere
with the main system!

00:40:59.550 --> 00:41:03.160
Hacking in now?
Could it be...

00:41:03.720 --> 00:41:06.460
Haseo, don't let go of her!

00:41:22.240 --> 00:41:23.780
They vanished!

00:41:24.210 --> 00:41:27.110
It got away. Master Yata?

00:41:27.550 --> 00:41:30.580
It must've found a hole in the security system.

00:41:31.020 --> 00:41:33.650
It looks like AIDA used that to get away.

00:41:34.020 --> 00:41:35.320
What about them?!

00:41:35.420 --> 00:41:39.330
I placed a tag onto Atoli's PC.

00:41:39.590 --> 00:41:43.260
Pi, Kuhn...l want you to go
and retrieve them right away.

00:41:43.360 --> 00:41:44.460
Yes!

00:41:51.510 --> 00:41:56.010
What are you thinking, Ovan?

00:42:06.890 --> 00:42:08.620
Atoli!

00:42:21.000 --> 00:42:23.240
These are Atoli's...?

00:42:24.470 --> 00:42:26.770
<i>So...how much did she get?</i>

00:42:26.870 --> 00:42:27.970
What's that?

00:42:28.640 --> 00:42:30.880
<i>5,000 yen!</i>

00:42:31.610 --> 00:42:35.960
<i>- Are you serious?! That's totally cheap!
- Sorry, that won't work for me...</i>

00:42:35.960 --> 00:42:38.480
<i>But that's not bad for a creepy old man.</i>

00:42:38.480 --> 00:42:40.120
<i>I bet it was
his whole allowance!</i>

00:42:40.290 --> 00:42:42.260
<i>That piddly amount of money!</i>

00:42:42.360 --> 00:42:44.820
<i>- So, what do you think?
- It gives me goose bumps!</i>

00:42:45.960 --> 00:42:50.800
- Are these Atoli's...? Atoli's memories?
<i>- Did she really do it?</i>

00:42:52.900 --> 00:42:54.630
<i>Yuck!</i>

00:43:20.330 --> 00:43:21.560
Atoli!

00:43:25.670 --> 00:43:28.500
I tried my best.

00:43:29.840 --> 00:43:32.510
I tried the best that I could.

00:43:33.510 --> 00:43:38.580
But it was no good.
It was no good no matter what I did.

00:43:39.010 --> 00:43:42.950
No matter how hard I tried,
everyone would reject me.

00:43:47.150 --> 00:43:49.690
No one cared about me.

00:43:51.090 --> 00:43:54.860
They rejected the real me!

00:44:06.840 --> 00:44:08.140
Atoli...

00:44:28.290 --> 00:44:30.160
Of all places...

00:44:37.670 --> 00:44:39.710
- We'd better get on with the recovery.
- Yeah.

00:44:42.480 --> 00:44:43.740
What's that?!

00:44:43.910 --> 00:44:49.020
That pattern! Don't tell me
she's also an Epitaph User?!

00:44:49.980 --> 00:44:53.990
AIDA and Epitaph Users...
You can't get a worse combination.

00:44:54.490 --> 00:44:57.090
What the hell?!
At this rate, Haseo will be destroyed!

00:44:57.420 --> 00:44:59.590
That's all right.

00:45:00.130 --> 00:45:01.200
- Huh?
- Huh?

00:45:21.680 --> 00:45:22.520
Atoli...

00:45:31.190 --> 00:45:34.630
You're all the same!
It's not fair!

00:45:35.030 --> 00:45:37.500
You just use me!

00:45:37.860 --> 00:45:41.700
You all blame me!
You take everything away from me!

00:45:44.900 --> 00:45:47.610
You're not doing this for me!

00:45:48.580 --> 00:45:51.610
You all just want to make it easy
on yourselves!

00:45:51.710 --> 00:45:57.450
You don't even think about it!
About how hard I tried! Or how hard I cried!

00:46:00.450 --> 00:46:04.220
How hard it was for me!

00:46:33.720 --> 00:46:38.490
I'm right here.
And I've always been here.

00:46:38.960 --> 00:46:43.000
But no one came looking for me.

00:46:45.570 --> 00:46:48.640
Didn't they know I was right here?!

00:46:53.470 --> 00:46:57.780
I'm right here, too.

00:46:59.680 --> 00:47:01.110
That's a lie!

00:47:24.200 --> 00:47:25.970
It's not a lie.

00:47:28.640 --> 00:47:30.510
It's not a lie.

00:47:32.410 --> 00:47:33.710
Atoli...

00:48:11.480 --> 00:48:17.460
<i>Hito no nami oshiyosete wa</i>
Pushing away the tides of people

00:48:17.590 --> 00:48:24.240
<i>Watashi wo kasume toori sugiru</i>
You walk right past me

00:48:24.460 --> 00:48:30.280
<i>itsudatte koko ni iru noni</i>
I am always right here

00:48:30.870 --> 00:48:36.720
<i>Nandaka nukegara</i>
But I feel so empty inside

00:48:37.280 --> 00:48:43.250
<i>Tada nagamete potsuri tatazumu</i>
I stand by myself, just gazing at you

00:48:43.620 --> 00:48:48.930
<i>Kodoku no hahen nomikonda</i>
And swallow a broken piece of loneliness

00:48:49.220 --> 00:48:55.700
<i>Hitori ni shinaide hanasanaide</i>
Don't leave me alone, don't let me go

00:48:55.930 --> 00:49:02.140
<i>Sono nukumori de tsutsunde</i>
Embrace me with your warmth

00:49:02.200 --> 00:49:08.520
<i>Kotoba wo kakete namae wo yonde</i>
Talk to me, call my name

00:49:08.810 --> 00:49:16.780
<i>Anata no namida hoho ni uketai</i>
Let your tear fall on my cheek

00:49:47.680 --> 00:49:54.000
<i>Kokoro no naka de sakendatte</i>
Even when I cry out inside my heart

00:49:54.320 --> 00:50:00.130
<i>Sono omoi wa todokanai</i>
That longing will never be heard

00:50:00.530 --> 00:50:06.500
<i>Ari no mama no watashi de irareruyou</i>
I want to hold your hand

00:50:06.700 --> 00:50:13.840
<i>Anata to te wo tsunaide itai</i>
So I can be my true self

00:50:14.370 --> 00:50:20.190
<i>Koe wo kikasete watashi wo mite</i>
Let me hear your voice, look at me

00:50:20.410 --> 00:50:26.060
<i>Sono hitomi ni utsushite</i>
Reflect me in your eyes

00:50:26.120 --> 00:50:32.430
<i>Anata ni furetai ude ni dakaretai</i>
I want to touch you, I want to be held by your arms

00:50:32.490 --> 00:50:40.310
<i>Anata no yubi de namida wo fuite</i>
Wipe my tears with your finger

00:50:40.570 --> 00:50:46.710
<i>Sono te de dakishimeraretara...</i>
If only I could be held...

00:50:46.770 --> 00:50:52.120
<i>...kitto</i>
...by those hands of yours

00:50:50.080 --> 00:50:51.020
Haseo...

00:50:52.510 --> 00:50:53.710
Yeah.

00:50:55.450 --> 00:50:56.420
I'm here.

00:50:56.950 --> 00:50:58.280
So am I.

00:50:59.920 --> 00:51:01.650
- We're here together.
- We're here together.

00:51:25.750 --> 00:51:27.050
Here.

00:51:38.060 --> 00:51:39.530
Where are we?

00:51:40.260 --> 00:51:41.490
Hi.

00:51:46.930 --> 00:51:50.770
Welcome back, Haseo.

00:51:56.010 --> 00:51:57.340
Ovan?

00:51:58.380 --> 00:52:01.650
Do you remember this place?

00:52:02.720 --> 00:52:07.890
Yeah, it's where you disappeared
six months ago.

00:52:11.190 --> 00:52:13.790
We have returned.

00:52:16.600 --> 00:52:18.600
To the place where it all began.

00:52:20.330 --> 00:52:24.600
Thus, we shall start again from this place.

00:52:25.970 --> 00:52:29.280
Start again? Start what?

00:52:31.310 --> 00:52:33.050
The demise!

00:52:41.350 --> 00:52:42.590
Haseo!

00:52:54.030 --> 00:52:57.170
What?! He was here?!

00:53:05.580 --> 00:53:06.880
Ovan?

00:53:07.410 --> 00:53:10.420
You don't seem to understand very well.

00:53:11.880 --> 00:53:16.490
Let me show you
how those scars are made, Haseo.

00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:17.960
Huh?

00:53:31.340 --> 00:53:33.470
There's no need for you to be frightened.

00:53:36.180 --> 00:53:38.280
Sear this into your brain!

00:53:57.360 --> 00:54:03.340
This is the truth that you have so desired!

00:54:30.930 --> 00:54:34.100
Haseo...

00:55:03.900 --> 00:55:05.600
Atoli?

00:55:11.740 --> 00:55:13.070
This can't be...right?

00:55:14.810 --> 00:55:19.150
This isn't real, is it?

00:55:31.220 --> 00:55:34.890
I was the one that killed Shino.

00:55:52.110 --> 00:55:55.180
Come after me, Haseo.

00:55:55.980 --> 00:55:58.820
When you manage to catch up...

00:55:58.980 --> 00:56:04.760
...your story will truly come to an end.

00:56:46.970 --> 00:56:50.870
Ovan!

00:57:13.790 --> 00:57:15.460
I've kept you waiting.

00:57:16.530 --> 00:57:19.170
He will come soon.

00:57:19.800 --> 00:57:22.600
Bringing with him
a hundred million origins...

00:57:23.070 --> 00:57:25.870
Bringing with him
a hundred million demises...

00:57:26.670 --> 00:57:29.540
To carry out his revenge of
one hundred million grudges...

00:57:29.640 --> 00:57:34.080
...he will come at me
with one hundred million fangs.

00:57:34.350 --> 00:57:37.780
Looking forward to it, aren't you?

00:57:38.480 --> 00:57:39.820
Ina?

00:57:51.500 --> 00:57:53.170
A Goddess?

00:57:53.810 --> 00:57:54.740
That's right.

00:57:55.860 --> 00:57:58.230
A goddess
that watches over "The World".

00:58:00.940 --> 00:58:03.280
Why did she go away?

00:58:04.480 --> 00:58:08.950
Maybe she ran out of patience.

00:58:09.050 --> 00:58:10.480
On what?

00:58:10.750 --> 00:58:12.590
On this world.

00:58:15.290 --> 00:58:18.490
I think it's something else.

00:58:18.490 --> 00:58:19.440
Hm?

00:58:23.030 --> 00:58:28.130
Even now, the goddess is
watching over this world.

00:58:29.870 --> 00:58:34.670
It's just that
she can't see all of the world from here.

00:58:35.540 --> 00:58:37.240
So she fled?

00:58:42.180 --> 00:58:45.780
A rather mischievous goddess, isn't she?

00:58:54.560 --> 00:58:56.730
What are you praying for?

00:59:02.840 --> 00:59:09.340
Hey, after I'm cured, I can still be with you
in the real world, right?

00:59:09.910 --> 00:59:11.040
Sure.

00:59:11.540 --> 00:59:12.880
Yay!

00:59:19.250 --> 00:59:22.350
I'll always be with you, Ina.

00:59:23.260 --> 00:59:25.190
We'll always be together.

00:59:29.430 --> 00:59:30.260
He's here.

01:00:18.240 --> 01:00:21.610
Welcome, Haseo!

01:00:34.360 --> 01:00:35.860
Is that your best?

01:00:38.000 --> 01:00:41.430
Your rage is weak.
You couldn't kill a fly.

01:02:30.440 --> 01:02:34.580
What's the matter? You're giving up
just because you lost your leg?

01:02:54.770 --> 01:02:56.070
This is mercy.

01:03:11.850 --> 01:03:13.220
Haseo...

01:03:19.090 --> 01:03:20.560
Haseo?

01:03:37.740 --> 01:03:39.210
<i>Atoli?</i>

01:03:43.750 --> 01:03:46.250
<i>Atoli, why are you...?</i>

01:03:46.920 --> 01:03:51.020
It's all right.
I am right here.

01:03:51.190 --> 01:03:53.590
I will be watching over you from here.

01:03:54.060 --> 01:03:58.260
I won't tell you not to grieve.
I won't tell you not to suffer.

01:03:59.100 --> 01:04:02.770
Because I know
what burden you are carrying.

01:04:03.440 --> 01:04:05.740
<i>Atoli, I</i>

01:04:05.840 --> 01:04:11.280
But I think it's time
you forgave yourself.

01:04:11.380 --> 01:04:14.180
You really tried hard, Haseo.

01:04:14.580 --> 01:04:18.480
<i>There's no point in trying
if it doesn't change the result.</i>

01:04:18.580 --> 01:04:24.520
But my heart is warm.
It's because you thought fondly of me.

01:04:24.790 --> 01:04:27.360
I can feel it pulsing right here.

01:04:27.890 --> 01:04:30.900
That in itself is a meaningful result.

01:04:31.700 --> 01:04:38.540
So it's not pointless
that you suffered and grieved.

01:04:38.670 --> 01:04:44.010
I can see that it has nurtured you,
and that that is now a part of you.

01:04:44.110 --> 01:04:45.580
<i>A part of me...</i>

01:05:11.300 --> 01:05:12.740
Haseo...

01:05:14.470 --> 01:05:17.140
What is it that you want to do?

01:05:17.240 --> 01:05:22.550
I want to save you.
And Shino, too.

01:05:25.720 --> 01:05:28.590
Ovan...

01:05:30.120 --> 01:05:32.590
Please save Ovan...

01:05:38.400 --> 01:05:39.340
I see...

01:05:41.200 --> 01:05:43.200
I get it.

01:06:03.290 --> 01:06:05.620
Let's go, Haseo.

01:06:06.590 --> 01:06:10.630
Yes, let's go.
Together.

01:06:30.750 --> 01:06:31.850
What's this?!

01:06:42.030 --> 01:06:43.230
Ovan...

01:06:46.300 --> 01:06:48.230
I want to save you!

01:06:50.170 --> 01:06:54.410
You think you can defeat me
with such childish sentiment?

01:06:55.670 --> 01:06:59.850
This is how I feel.
This is my wish.

01:07:00.780 --> 01:07:04.920
I will no longer be the Terror of Death!

01:07:08.350 --> 01:07:11.520
All right, then.
You want to test yourself?

01:07:21.430 --> 01:07:23.340
Go!

01:07:32.080 --> 01:07:33.280
Ovan!

01:07:38.750 --> 01:07:40.220
That pattern!

01:07:42.050 --> 01:07:46.260
Now, this is where it begins.
Haseo!

01:07:46.360 --> 01:07:49.130
Fine! Come! Come at me!

01:07:49.800 --> 01:07:50.830
Come! Rebirth!

01:07:51.230 --> 01:07:52.530
I am right here!

01:07:52.730 --> 01:07:53.900
Corbenik!

01:07:54.330 --> 01:07:56.500
Skeith!

01:08:07.250 --> 01:08:08.350
Ovan!

01:08:17.560 --> 01:08:19.960
You taught me everything!

01:08:23.460 --> 01:08:26.200
You gave me power!

01:08:26.530 --> 01:08:31.470
You were where I belonged!

01:09:03.100 --> 01:09:05.070
This time it's my turn!

01:09:08.040 --> 01:09:10.140
I will save you!

01:09:12.110 --> 01:09:13.810
I will find you!

01:09:20.520 --> 01:09:24.390
I will be the place where
you belong!

01:09:44.340 --> 01:09:48.280
That's what I've decided!

01:10:11.040 --> 01:10:12.440
Brother?

01:10:13.870 --> 01:10:15.310
Brother?

01:10:17.210 --> 01:10:18.810
Hey, Brother!

01:10:18.910 --> 01:10:20.410
Uh, what?

01:10:20.550 --> 01:10:23.150
Were you listening to my story?

01:10:24.050 --> 01:10:27.750
Oh, I'm sorry.
I had something on my mind.

01:10:27.850 --> 01:10:31.490
You're always like that. And we finally
got to spend some time together.

01:10:31.620 --> 01:10:34.160
I wish you'd just forget about other things
for the moment.

01:10:34.260 --> 01:10:37.830
It's like I'm the only one enjoying this.

01:10:40.030 --> 01:10:43.800
I was only thinking about you, Ina.

01:10:45.000 --> 01:10:48.180
I will soon have completed
a big part of my work.

01:10:48.240 --> 01:10:49.640
And then...

01:10:51.080 --> 01:10:52.840
...I'll be sure to come and get you.

01:10:53.780 --> 01:10:55.950
And we can live together.

01:10:56.050 --> 01:10:56.880
Really?!

01:11:06.390 --> 01:11:07.560
What's the matter?

01:11:10.030 --> 01:11:11.830
Uh, Brother?

01:11:14.030 --> 01:11:16.640
Oh, it's nothing.

01:11:21.140 --> 01:11:22.210
Ina!

01:11:28.180 --> 01:11:29.010
Brother!

01:11:51.540 --> 01:11:53.670
Ina...!

01:12:19.730 --> 01:12:21.230
Ovan?

01:12:24.870 --> 01:12:27.410
This is as it should be.

01:12:34.380 --> 01:12:35.780
Who's that girl?

01:12:36.010 --> 01:12:39.420
That's Ina, the very
first to become comatose.

01:12:39.520 --> 01:12:41.950
She also happens to be my little sister.

01:12:42.220 --> 01:12:43.660
Sister?

01:12:47.960 --> 01:12:49.360
What do you mean?

01:12:50.960 --> 01:12:56.870
AIDA's identity is an Al parasite
that infects electric signals.

01:12:57.870 --> 01:13:03.110
When this parasite infects
an ordinary program, there's little damage.

01:13:03.640 --> 01:13:07.250
But when it's a human...

01:13:07.510 --> 01:13:09.380
Why would it affect a human?

01:13:09.880 --> 01:13:14.250
Human consciousness is nothing
but a product of electric signals.

01:13:16.190 --> 01:13:21.230
When one is infected by AIDA,
normal function of consciousness is inhibited.

01:13:21.330 --> 01:13:24.000
That's the cause of
the loss of consciousness?

01:13:24.400 --> 01:13:27.700
AIDA possesses a strong life force.

01:13:28.000 --> 01:13:33.640
In order to defeat it,
there is but one special method.

01:13:34.910 --> 01:13:38.580
In other words, "Rebirth".

01:13:39.040 --> 01:13:41.150
Rebirth?

01:13:41.410 --> 01:13:46.420
My power is the ability
to purify all of the data in the network.

01:13:49.120 --> 01:13:53.790
But the use of that power was impossible
with just my will.

01:13:54.830 --> 01:13:57.830
I needed you, Haseo.

01:13:58.160 --> 01:14:02.430
I needed your will.
A strong desire that is beyond my ability.

01:14:02.530 --> 01:14:03.900
That is exactly...

01:14:04.070 --> 01:14:07.570
The condition required to initiate
the rebirth?

01:14:20.890 --> 01:14:21.650
Ovan?

01:14:32.460 --> 01:14:33.630
Ina...

01:14:46.010 --> 01:14:47.050
Ovan...?

01:14:55.890 --> 01:15:01.330
Awaken, Ina!
Now's your time to be free!

01:17:15.430 --> 01:17:16.930
Damn! Damn! Damn! Damn!

01:17:17.160 --> 01:17:23.900
Damn!

01:17:24.600 --> 01:17:25.940
Ovan!

01:18:05.310 --> 01:18:06.480
Haseo...

01:18:08.610 --> 01:18:11.620
Atoli, I never...

01:18:12.720 --> 01:18:16.020
I never wanted it to end like this!

01:18:19.690 --> 01:18:25.560
Ovan just wanted to save his little sister.
And maybe he's satisfied with that!

01:18:25.900 --> 01:18:31.370
But who else could appreciate that
other than Ovan himself?!

01:18:32.240 --> 01:18:35.770
Ovan's sister's and Shino's
consciousnesses are finally restored...

01:18:36.270 --> 01:18:41.350
...but what's the point if someone
so precious to them is gone?!

01:18:41.450 --> 01:18:44.280
There's no happiness in that!

01:18:45.080 --> 01:18:50.020
I can't have that!
I can't let it end that way!

01:18:50.420 --> 01:18:51.460
That's why...!

01:18:51.560 --> 01:18:53.420
Please go and get him.

01:18:55.160 --> 01:18:58.360
I can help with my Epitaph.

01:18:58.600 --> 01:19:03.400
It can feel the emotions flowing through
the world, and bring them together as one.

01:19:03.570 --> 01:19:05.770
That is my power.

01:19:05.870 --> 01:19:07.310
You're also...?

01:19:09.510 --> 01:19:12.610
The feelings you have for Ovan...

01:19:12.910 --> 01:19:15.180
His sister's feelings...

01:19:15.250 --> 01:19:17.150
Shino's feelings...

01:19:17.850 --> 01:19:20.720
That's not all.

01:19:21.990 --> 01:19:27.690
All the feelings and sentiments
that Ovan inspired in many people.

01:19:28.190 --> 01:19:31.760
Please convey them to Ovan.

01:19:31.900 --> 01:19:33.000
Yeah.

01:19:56.820 --> 01:19:59.920
Get it back! All of it!

01:20:38.600 --> 01:20:40.600
<i>He's calling.</i>

01:20:44.440 --> 01:20:47.240
<i>Listen, he's calling you.</i>

01:20:51.140 --> 01:20:52.440
Who is it?

01:20:53.910 --> 01:20:58.650
Ovan! Ovan!

01:21:00.320 --> 01:21:01.650
Ovan!

01:21:28.180 --> 01:21:29.510
Haseo...

01:21:31.480 --> 01:21:34.320
<i>Small children of Morganna...</i>

01:21:34.550 --> 01:21:35.530
Huh?

01:21:37.320 --> 01:21:38.460
Who is that?!

01:21:40.490 --> 01:21:46.060
I'd say that it's the Goddess.
In other words, the world itself.

01:21:47.400 --> 01:21:51.740
<i>Punishment for crimes...
Compensation for miracles...</i>

01:21:52.100 --> 01:21:57.110
<i>That is the foundation of this world.
An absolute principle of order.</i>

01:21:59.680 --> 01:22:03.780
You fool! What compensation?!
What foundation?!

01:22:03.950 --> 01:22:07.720
Don't go along with that!
Don't let it be true!

01:22:07.820 --> 01:22:12.720
It's because you sum it up that way,
that I have to...!

01:22:23.730 --> 01:22:26.740
Don't give up! Don't let go!

01:22:26.840 --> 01:22:30.740
I'm right here!
I'm watching over you from right here!

01:22:33.440 --> 01:22:37.550
And it's not just me!
There's your sister, and Shino!

01:22:37.650 --> 01:22:41.250
Everyone's watching over you!

01:22:41.820 --> 01:22:43.520
Ovan!

01:22:46.990 --> 01:22:50.130
I will convey their feelings to you!
I will let you hear them!

01:23:17.720 --> 01:23:20.190
Accept it!

01:23:30.600 --> 01:23:35.540
<i>A strong wish is what can
change the world.</i>

01:23:56.960 --> 01:23:58.330
Uh, excuse me!

01:24:17.350 --> 01:24:18.750
I'm sorry!

01:24:27.760 --> 01:24:29.460
You're late.

01:24:30.490 --> 01:24:33.500
I'm sorry. I got tied up.

01:24:33.830 --> 01:24:35.130
Tied up?

01:24:37.330 --> 01:24:40.000
Um, are you mad at me?

01:24:40.270 --> 01:24:41.170
Not really.

01:24:43.010 --> 01:24:45.280
Oh! I'm sorry! I'm really sorry!

01:25:04.060 --> 01:25:05.560
It's so peaceful.

01:25:08.100 --> 01:25:09.270
Yes.

01:25:10.940 --> 01:25:17.270
It all seems like a dream now.
AIDA and Tri-Edge and such.

01:25:17.610 --> 01:25:21.050
Yes.
But that was...

01:25:21.350 --> 01:25:23.810
Yeah. It was real.

01:25:34.930 --> 01:25:36.160
Atoli?

01:25:36.490 --> 01:25:37.630
Yes?

01:25:41.800 --> 01:25:43.170
Uh...Um, you know...

01:25:51.980 --> 01:25:54.780
I hope I didn't interrupt anything.

01:25:55.380 --> 01:25:56.780
Sh-Shino?

01:25:58.980 --> 01:26:01.590
It's been a long time.

01:26:01.690 --> 01:26:03.490
How did you know to come here?

01:26:04.020 --> 01:26:06.690
Atoli told me.

01:26:07.490 --> 01:26:08.470
Huh?

01:26:16.370 --> 01:26:19.100
I wanted to thank you properly.

01:26:25.140 --> 01:26:26.640
Thank you.

01:26:27.750 --> 01:26:28.880
What?!

01:26:29.650 --> 01:26:32.880
You kept your promise.

01:26:34.990 --> 01:26:39.020
That's all I wanted to say.

01:26:39.620 --> 01:26:41.690
Shino, I...

01:26:42.690 --> 01:26:45.030
It's all right. I know.

01:26:49.200 --> 01:26:51.800
I'm counting on you
to watch out for Haseo.

01:26:55.070 --> 01:26:56.340
Yes.

01:26:57.440 --> 01:26:59.610
I'll leave you then.

01:27:04.820 --> 01:27:05.950
Shino!

01:27:08.050 --> 01:27:09.190
Hm?

01:27:56.830 --> 01:27:58.070
Thank you.

01:28:02.840 --> 01:28:07.650
<i>Tsumetai te ni hiki yoserare</i>
Attracted by an icy cold hand

01:28:07.910 --> 01:28:12.550
<i>Nagarete yuku toki wo sugoshi</i>
I pass time as it flows on and on

01:28:12.980 --> 01:28:17.630
<i>Tooku wo mita sono hitomi ni</i>
As your eyes look into the distance

01:28:18.020 --> 01:28:22.660
<i>Nani ga utsutte iru no darou</i>
What is reflected in them

01:28:25.600 --> 01:28:29.910
<i>Tsuki ga terasu tsumetai yubi ni</i>
The moon shines on my bitter cold fingers

01:28:30.630 --> 01:28:35.640
<i>Koboreta no wa tsumetai namida</i>
And my icy tears fall onto them

01:28:35.710 --> 01:28:40.350
<i>Miageta sora itsuka no yume ga</i>
Looking up at the sky, a dream of long ago

01:28:40.780 --> 01:28:45.920
<i>Tooku de mitsumete iru</i>
Is waiting far in the distance

01:28:48.350 --> 01:28:52.990
<i>Kurayami ni te wo sashi nobete</i>
Reaching out into the darkness

01:28:53.360 --> 01:28:58.170
<i>Koko kara wa mou modorenai</i>
Not being able to turn back

01:28:58.400 --> 01:29:03.040
<i>Ki ga tsukeba kioku no naka ni</i>
I noticed myself

01:29:03.800 --> 01:29:09.110
<i>Tozasareta watashi ga mieta</i>
Closed up in my memories

01:29:10.910 --> 01:29:15.980
<i>Shinjite itai anata ga kuru no wo</i>
I want to believe that you will return

01:29:16.080 --> 01:29:20.720
<i>Itsu no hi ka koko de meguriau made</i>
Until we meet here one day

01:29:21.150 --> 01:29:26.120
<i>Kanjite itai toki ga tomaru made</i>
I want to keep feeling until the end of time

01:29:26.220 --> 01:29:31.870
<i>Atatakai te de watashi ni furete</i>
The warm touch of your hands

01:29:32.600 --> 01:29:37.410
<i>Garasu no ori ni torawarete ita</i>
Trapped inside this transparent cage

01:29:37.600 --> 01:29:42.410
<i>Tokenai omoi kizu tsuita mama</i>
I can't free my hurt feelings

01:29:42.640 --> 01:29:47.590
<i>Modoru koto nai kurayami no mukou</i>
Beyond the eternal darkness

01:29:47.640 --> 01:29:53.290
<i>Hikari ga sashite iru darou</i>
I know there is light shining through

01:30:13.600 --> 01:30:18.420
<i>Kitto mata koboreru hikari</i>
I know that your abundant light

01:30:18.680 --> 01:30:23.490
<i>Atatakaku tsutsunde kureru</i>
Will wrap me in warmth

01:30:23.680 --> 01:30:28.650
<i>Genjitsu Kara nigeyou to shite</i>
Trying to escape from reality

01:30:29.050 --> 01:30:34.370
<i>Daiji na mono miushinatteru</i>
I have lost sight of what is most important

01:30:34.930 --> 01:30:39.900
<i>Shinjite itai anata ga kuru no wo</i>
I want to believe that you will return

01:30:40.030 --> 01:30:44.840
<i>Itsu no hi ka koko de meguriau made</i>
Until we meet here one day

01:30:45.200 --> 01:30:50.020
<i>Kanjite itai toki ga tomaru made</i>
I want to keep feeling until the end of time

01:30:50.210 --> 01:30:55.850
<i>Atatakai te de watashi ni furete</i>
The warm touch of your hands

01:30:56.510 --> 01:31:01.490
<i>Tsumetai te ni hiki yoserare</i>
Attracted by an icy cold hand

01:31:01.590 --> 01:31:06.560
<i>Nagarete yuku toki wo sugoshi</i>
I pass time as it flows on and on

01:31:06.690 --> 01:31:11.660
<i>Tooku wo mita sono hitomi ni</i>
As your eyes look into the distance

01:31:11.730 --> 01:31:16.540
<i>Nani ga utsutte iru no darou</i>
What is reflected in them

01:32:00.840 --> 01:32:02.880
Brother!

01:32:43.720 --> 01:32:49.430
The menace has been dealt with.
The situation is as predicted.

01:32:49.530 --> 01:32:53.160
<i>I suppose it's not possible
to resist the will of Heaven.</i>

01:32:53.530 --> 01:32:56.500
<i>What are the people of Schicksal up to?</i>

01:32:56.600 --> 01:33:00.940
They have already moved on to
the next phase.

01:33:02.310 --> 01:33:05.040
<i>Give the oar to the ferryman.</i>

01:33:05.410 --> 01:33:07.840
I'll do as you say.

01:33:18.190 --> 01:33:23.130
<i>Prisoners of Karon!</i>
